# Stifle: "Counter target activated or triggered ability" (CR 701.6, 115.1). While Bot2's Flametongue Kavu is a spell on the
# stack, paid for with mana abilities (which never use the stack, CR 605.3a), there is no ability for Stifle to target and Bot1
# can't cast it (the refusal). Once the Kavu enters, its "deals 4 damage to target creature" triggers aimed at Bot1's
# Ornithopter; Bot1 Stifles that (the positive control): the ability is countered and does nothing, and the Kavu stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Ornithopter
Stifle
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Flametongue Kavu
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Flametongue Kavu.Cast
? Stack = Flametongue Kavu
! Bot1.Hand.Stifle.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Target(Ornithopter)
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Stifle.Cast(Stack.Flametongue Kavu)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Damage = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Stifle
Bot2.Battlefield = Mountain; Flametongue Kavu
